# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# A multiple regression gives y-hat = 6.3 + 0.3 x1 - 0.8 x2. The sample means of the independent variables are x1-bar = 12.4 and x2-bar = 4.5. What is the sample mean y-bar? (round to the hundredths)
# Hint: the OLS regression passes through the point of means: y-bar = beta0 + beta1 * x1-bar + beta2 * x2-bar. Here beta2 is negative.
b0    <- 6.3        # edit
b1    <- 0.3        # edit
b2    <- -0.8       # edit
x1bar <- 12.4       # edit
x2bar <- 4.5        # edit
round(b0 + b1 * x1bar + b2 * x2bar, 2)   # 6.42
# Opposite direction (given y-bar, solve for an intercept): b0 <- ybar - b1 * x1bar - b2 * x2bar

