# Hint: Table 3.2: Bias(beta1-tilde) = beta2 * delta1-tilde, and delta1-tilde has the sign of Cor(X1, X2).
# ANSWER: biased upward   (negative x negative = positive bias)
# Full table, in case he flips it:
#   beta2 < 0, correlation negative -> biased UPWARD
#   beta2 < 0, correlation positive -> biased DOWNWARD
#   beta2 > 0, correlation negative -> biased DOWNWARD
#   beta2 > 0, correlation positive -> biased UPWARD
#   beta2 = 0 or correlation = 0    -> UNBIASED
# (same signs = upward, different signs = downward)

